# Reversing a Singly Linked List in C

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

typedef struct Node {
    int data;
    struct Node *next;
} Node;

/**
 * Reverses a singly linked list in place.
 * 
 * @param head  Pointer to the current head of the list.
 * @return      Pointer to the new head (previously the tail).
 *
 * Time complexity:  O(n)
 * Space complexity: O(1)  — no extra nodes allocated.
 */
Node *reverse_list(Node *head)
{
    Node *prev = NULL;
    Node *curr = head;
    Node *next = NULL;

    while (curr != NULL) {
        next = curr->next;   /* save the rest of the list */
        curr->next = prev;   /* reverse the link */
        prev = curr;         /* advance prev */
        curr = next;         /* advance curr */
    }

    return prev;             /* prev is the new head */
}
```

